use flake

# Puts the release build of `jot` on PATH inside this repo, so the CLI can be dogfooded by name
# rather than by path. direnv exports environment only — it cannot define a shell alias — so this
# is the PATH equivalent of `alias jot=./target/release/jot`, and it works in scripts and
# subshells too.
#
# `jot` is therefore whatever `cargo build --release` last produced. Rebuild after changing the
# code, or run `cargo run -p jot-cli -- <args>` when iterating. Only the release directory is added,
# deliberately: adding target/debug as well would make which binary you just ran depend on PATH
# order, which is exactly the confusion worth avoiding while dogfooding.
PATH_add target/release
